source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_graphical(&refusal)
---
safix::unknown_name

  × 'no-such-secret' is not a secret flake.safix.users.alice holds.
  │ 
  │ A secret is declared in exactly one of three places, and this resolves
  │ the owning file from all three:
  │ 
  │   1. flake.safix.catalogue.no-such-secret — the shared catalogue —
  │ selected by
  │      flake.safix.users.alice.carries.no-such-secret
  │   2. flake.safix.users.alice.private.no-such-secret — this user's own
  │ entry
  │   3. flake.safix.users.<owner>.sharedWith.alice.no-such-secret — granted
  │ from outside
  │ 
  │ Declare it in one of them, then re-run. A name reaching a set only
  │ through a perHost.<host> or perTag.<tag> add or force is refused here
  │ too: placement is derived from those three sources alone, and the
  │ per-host and per-tag scopes sit outside it deliberately, because they
  │ adjust a secret for one machine rather than declare who holds it. One
  │ file serves every host that resolves the secret, so a value set through
  │ a single host's adjustment would apply everywhere that secret
  │ resolves rather than only where the adjustment does.
  │ 
  │ Names flake.safix.users.alice holds:
  │   - alice-alone
  │   - team-vault
